leek16 ISA Specification
========================

1. Overview

Word size:       16 bits
Registers:       8 x 16 bit general purpose
Address Width:   16 bits
Memory:          64 KiB (2^16)
Reset PC:        0x0000

2. Registers

R0-7:      16 bit general purpose
PC:        16 bit program counter
SP:        16 bit stack pointer
CND:       1 bit condition flag

Register fields are 3 bits. They hold R0-R7 only.
Only RDSP, WRSP and RDPC use SP and PC (section 7.4).
Comparisons write CND. BRT and BRF read CND.

3. Memory Layout

Memory spans the full 16 bit address space.

	0x0000 - 0xFFFF

Memory is byte addressable. 16 bit values are big-endian.

Example:

	16 bit instruction layout
	instruction = 0x1234
	address @ 0x1000 = 0x12
	address @ 0x1001 = 0x34

4.  Standard Instruction Format

A standard instruction is 16 bits (one word).

15               8        5        2        0
+----------------+--------+--------+--------+
|     OPCODE     |   RD   |   RS1  |  RS2   |
+----------------+--------+--------+--------+
      7 bits          3        3        3

Unused fields MUST be 0.


5.  Immediate Instruction Format

An immediate instruction is 32 bits (two words).

First word:

15               8        5        2    0
+----------------+--------+--------+----+---+
|     OPCODE     |   RD   |   RS   |RESV|ORD|
+----------------+--------+--------+----+---+
      7 bits          3        3      2    1

RESV MUST be 0.

ORD is the operand order. Only ADDI, SUBI, ANDI, ORI, SHLI, SHRI and CMPI use ORD.

	ORD = 0:   register on the left    R1 := R2 - 5
	ORD = 1:   constant on the left    R1 := 5 - R2

In other immediate instructions, ORD MUST be 0.
Unused fields MUST be 0.

Second word:

15                                          0
+-------------------------------------------+
|                 Immediate                 |
+-------------------------------------------+
                 16 bits


After a standard instruction:
PC += 2 (for 2 bytes, 16 bits)

After an immediate instruction:
PC += 4 (for 4 bytes, 32 bits)

6. Constants and Functions

Constants:

	Decimal:       1234
	Hexadecimal:   0x04D2
	Range:         0 - 65535 (0x0000 - 0xFFFF)

Functions:

	FUNC name:
		...
	END

A function is the address of the next instruction.
Each function name must be unique.

7. Instructions

7.1 Data Movement

MOV
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2

	Operation:
		R1 = R2

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2

	Length:
		16 bits

LOADI
	Syntax:
		R1 := 0x1234

	Operation:
		R1 = IMM16

	Fields:
		RD = R1, IMM16 = 0x1234

	Length:
		32 bits

LOADR
	Syntax:
		R1 <- [R2]
		[R2] -> R1

	Operation:
		R1 = MEMORY[R2]

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2

	Length:
		16 bits

LOADA
	Syntax:
		R1 <- [0x1000]
		[0x1000] -> R1

	Operation:
		R1 = MEMORY[IMM16]

	Fields:
		RD = R1, IMM16 = 0x1000

	Length:
		32 bits

STORER
	Syntax:
		R1 -> [R2]
		[R2] <- R1

	Operation:
		MEMORY[R2] = R1

	Fields:
		RS1 = R2, RS2 = R1

	Length:
		16 bits

STOREI
	Syntax:
		5 -> [R2]
		[R2] <- 5

	Operation:
		MEMORY[R2] = IMM16

	Fields:
		RS = R2, IMM16 = 5

	Length:
		32 bits

STOREA
	Syntax:
		R1 -> [0x1000]
		[0x1000] <- R1

	Operation:
		MEMORY[IMM16] = R1

	Fields:
		RS = R1, IMM16 = 0x1000

	Length:
		32 bits

7.2 Arithmetic and Logic

ADD
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 + R3

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 + R3

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2, RS2 = R3

	Length:
		16 bits

ADDI
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 + 5
		R1 := 5 + R2

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 + IMM16

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS = R2, IMM16 = 5, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

SUB
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 - R3

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 - R3

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2, RS2 = R3

	Length:
		16 bits

SUBI
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 - 5
		R1 := 5 - R2

	Operation:
		if ORD == 0:
			R1 = R2 - IMM16
		if ORD == 1:
			R1 = IMM16 - R2

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS = R2, IMM16 = 5, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

AND
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 & R3

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 & R3

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2, RS2 = R3

	Length:
		16 bits

ANDI
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 & 5
		R1 := 5 & R2

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 & IMM16

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS = R2, IMM16 = 5, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

OR
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 | R3

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 | R3

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2, RS2 = R3

	Length:
		16 bits

ORI
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 | 5
		R1 := 5 | R2

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 | IMM16

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS = R2, IMM16 = 5, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

NOT
	Syntax:
		R1 := !R2

	Operation:
		R1 = NOT R2 (bitwise)

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2

	Length:
		16 bits

SHL
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 << R3

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 << R3

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2, RS2 = R3

	Length:
		16 bits

SHLI
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 << 4
		R1 := 4 << R2

	Operation:
		if ORD == 0:
			R1 = R2 << IMM16
		if ORD == 1:
			R1 = IMM16 << R2

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS = R2, IMM16 = 4, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

SHR
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 >> R3

	Operation:
		R1 = R2 >> R3 (logical)

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS1 = R2, RS2 = R3

	Length:
		16 bits

SHRI
	Syntax:
		R1 := R2 >> 4
		R1 := 4 >> R2

	Operation:
		if ORD == 0:
			R1 = R2 >> IMM16 (logical)
		if ORD == 1:
			R1 = IMM16 >> R2 (logical)

	Fields:
		RD = R1, RS = R2, IMM16 = 4, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

7.3 Comparisons

A comparison sets CND to 1 if it is true, and to 0 if it is false.
Comparisons use unsigned 16 bit values.
Each comparison operator has a different opcode.

CMP
	Syntax:
		R1 == R2
		R1 != R2
		R1 > R2
		R1 < R2
		R1 >= R2
		R1 <= R2

	Operation:
		CND = (R1 op R2)

	Fields:
		RS1 = R1, RS2 = R2

	Length:
		16 bits

CMPI
	Syntax:
		R1 == 5
		R1 != 5
		R1 > 5
		R1 < 5
		R1 >= 5
		R1 <= 5
		5 == R1
		5 != R1
		5 > R1
		5 < R1
		5 >= R1
		5 <= R1

	Operation:
		if ORD == 0:
			CND = (R1 op IMM16)
		if ORD == 1:
			CND = (IMM16 op R1)

	Fields:
		RS = R1, IMM16 = 5, ORD = 0 or 1

	Length:
		32 bits

7.4 Special Registers

RDSP
	Syntax:
		R1 := SP

	Operation:
		R1 = SP

	Fields:
		RD = R1

	Length:
		16 bits

WRSP
	Syntax:
		SP := R1

	Operation:
		SP = R1

	Fields:
		RS1 = R1

	Length:
		16 bits

RDPC
	Syntax:
		R1 := PC

	Operation:
		R1 = address(this instruction)

	Fields:
		RD = R1

	Length:
		16 bits

7.5 Control Flow

JMP
	Syntax:
		JMP LABEL

	Operation:
		PC = address(LABEL)

	Fields:
		IMM16 = address(LABEL)

	Length:
		32 bits

BRT
	Syntax:
		BRT LABEL

	Operation:
		if CND == 1:
			PC = address(LABEL)

	Fields:
		IMM16 = address(LABEL)

	Length:
		32 bits

BRF
	Syntax:
		BRF LABEL

	Operation:
		if CND == 0:
			PC = address(LABEL)

	Fields:
		IMM16 = address(LABEL)

	Length:
		32 bits

8. Assembler Expansions

The assembler calculates operations on two constants.

	R1 := 5 + 3

becomes:

	R1 := 8          (LOADI, 32 bits)

The assembler truncates the result to 16 bits.

9. Invalid Forms

The assembler rejects these forms.

	5 <- [R2]          Load into a constant.
	[R2] -> 5          Load into a constant.
	5 -> [0x1000]      Store a constant to a constant address.
	5 > 3              Compare two constants.
	PC := R1           Write to PC. Use JMP.
	R1 := SP + 2       SP or PC in an instruction other than RDSP, WRSP or RDPC.

10. Reset/Boot

On reset:

	PC = 0x0000
	SP = 0xFFFE
	CND = 0

Execution starts at address 0x0000.
